  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/ariidae/ketengus_typus.htm",
      "html": "<ul><li>Common name: Bigmouth sea catfish</li><li>Synonym: Pimelodus pectinidens</li><li>IUCN Red List: Not Evaluated</li></ul><p>Teeth are absent from the roof of the mouth, and the mouth opens wide, extending far beyond the eye. Only one species is recorded (monotypic genus).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/ariidae/ketengus_typus.htm",
      "html": "<p>Asia: Eastern Bay of Bengal and Malay Peninsula; in nearshore coastal waters, estuaries, and lower reaches of rivers (Kailola, 1999). Occurs in coastal waters from Thailand to Indonesia and westward to the Andaman Islands. Type locality: Banjarmasin, in rivers (in fluviis).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/ariidae/ketengus_typus.htm",
      "html": "<p>Found in the lower parts of rivers in either fresh or brackish waters.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/ariidae/ketengus_typus.htm",
      "html": "<p>Feeds on invertebrates and small fishes.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/ariidae/ketengus_typus.htm",
      "html": "<p>Etymology: The genus name Ketengus is a latinisation of Keteng, the Madurese name for this catfish in eastern Java, Indonesia. The specific name typus means serving as type of the genus.</p><p>Remarks: Caught with trawls, seines, and traps.</p>"
    }
  ],
